  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Geneva Call 2024-2026</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Geneva Call 2024-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Geneva Call har ans&#xF6;kt till Sida om k&#xE4;rnst&#xF6;d om 14,8 miljoner kr f&#xF6;r perioden 1 oktober 2024- 31 december 2026 (2 miljoner kr 2024 och 6,4 miljoner kr f&#xF6;r 2025 och 2026 vardera) f&#xF6;r att genomf&#xF6;ra organisationens &#xF6;vergripande strategiska plan. Sida f&#xF6;rl&#xE4;ngde det tidigare avtalet fram till 31 september 2024, med 4,4 miljoner kr, varav Sidas totala st&#xF6;d f&#xF6;r 2024 ocks&#xE5; uppg&#xE5;r till 6,4 miljoner kr.

Den strategiska planen anger Geneva Calls humanit&#xE4;ra engagemang med icke-statliga v&#xE4;pnade akt&#xF6;rer i syfte att st&#xE4;rka skydd av civila i konfliktkontexter. De nu g&#xE4;llande tematiska omr&#xE5;dena &#xE4;r f&#xF6;rbud mot antipersonella minor och samarbete kring minhantering, skydd av barn fr&#xE5;n effekter av v&#xE4;pnad konflikt, f&#xF6;rbud mot sexuellt v&#xE5;ld i v&#xE4;pnade konflikter and mot elimineringen av k&#xF6;nsdiskriminering, skydd av h&#xE4;lsov&#xE5;rd i v&#xE4;pnade konflikter, samt f&#xF6;rebyggande av sv&#xE4;lt och konfliktrelaterat  matos&#xE4;kerhet. Organisationen &#xE4;r f&#xF6;r n&#xE4;rvarande aktiv i 14 konflikt kontexter och har n&#xE4;rvaro i Jemen (Aden), Syrien, Irak, Colombia, Afghanistan, Myanmar, Filippinerna, Ukraina, Mali, DRK (Goma), Libyen, Sydsudan och Thailand f&#xF6;r att arbeta regionalt med Myanmar. De har &#xE4;ven ett satellit kontor i Bryssel.

Geneva Call:s totala budget f&#xF6;r perioden &#xE4;r ca 804 miljoner kr. Sidas k&#xE4;rnst&#xF6;d t&#xE4;cker d&#xE4;rmed cirka 2,5 procent av det totala behovet per &#xE5;r och tillsammans med Norge,  Irland, och Spanien t&#xE4;cker Sida cirka 14 procent av k&#xE4;rnst&#xF6;det. De st&#xF6;rsta givarna under 2024 &#xE4;r EU (30 %), Norge (20.2%), UK (19.2 %), Tyskland (7.1%) and Schweiz (5.3 %).</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Geneva Call has applied to Sida for core support of SEK 14.8 million for the period October 1, 2024- December 31, 2026 (SEK 2 million in 2024 and SEK 6.4 million for 2025 and 2026 each) to implement the organization&apos;s overall strategic plan. Sida extended the previous agreement until 31 September 2024, with SEK 4.4 million, thus Sida&apos;s total support for 2024 also amounts to SEK 6.4 million. 

The strategic plan sets out Geneva Call&apos;s humanitarian engagement with non-state armed actors to strengthen the protection of civilians in conflict contexts. The current thematic areas are the prohibition of anti-personnel mines and cooperation on mine management, the protection of children from the effects of armed conflict, the prohibition of sexual violence in armed conflicts and the elimination of gender discrimination, the protection of health care in armed conflicts, and the prevention of famine and conflict-related food insecurity. The organization is currently active in 14 conflict contexts and has presence in Yemen (Aden), Syria, Iraq, Colombia, Afghanistan, Myanmar, Philippines, Ukraine, Mali, DRC (Goma), Libya, South Sudan and Thailand to work regionally with Myanmar. They also have a satellite office in Brussels. 

Geneva Call&apos;s total budget for the period is approx. SEK 804 million. Sida&apos;s core support thus covers approximately 2.5 percent of the total need per year, and together with Norway, Ireland and Spain, Sida covers approximately 14 percent of the core support. The largest donors in 2024 are the EU (30%), Norway (20.2%), the UK (19.2%), Germany (7.1%) and Switzerland (5.3%).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with the Geneva Call 2024-2027 Strategic Plan, the overall objectives of the Core Activities are:
1.To champion Armed Groups and De Facto Authorities (AGDAs) application of International Humanitarian Law (IHL)
2.To reinforce and create fit-for-purpose engagement tools to enhance AGDAs application of IHL
3.To cultivate the universality of humanitarian norms and principles
4.To respond to growing operational imperatives with a balanced, strategic approach and secured resources.</narrative>
  </description>
